    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter tonight\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** providing the clear anchor for the lineup; his 87.42 score against the hittable Me. Kelly (5.23 xERA) is bolstered by an elite 0.451 xwOBA and a prime #2 hole placement, making him the highest-ceiling asset in the rotation. Close behind is **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12), whose leadoff assignment against the soft-tossing Junk (4.64 xERA) maximizes his stolen base potential, an area where our league strategy demands elite sprint-speed utility. **Christian Yelich** (74.33) also projects as an elite play; his matchup against Lowder is complemented by a rare \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus, further incentivizing his presence in the outfield as we hunt for critical SBs. \n\nOn the bench, **Jacob Gonzalez** (50.42) was the most difficult exclusion, finishing within a fraction of **Pedro Ramirez** (50.53). The optimizer ultimately favored **Pedro Ramirez** due to the higher SP skill projection (4.64 xERA vs 5.35) and the strategic benefit of switch-hitting flexibility, even though **Jacob Gonzalez** arguably holds a safer floor. We are managing several lineup risks tonight, as both **Junior Caminero** and **Kazuma Okamoto** are currently marked as \"Lineup Pending.\" While **Junior Caminero** remains a start at 55.11 despite facing a respectable arm in Williams, any official drop in the batting order would likely require a re-evaluation of our bench depth, particularly if **Colt Keith** or **Josh Smith** receive confirmation of a higher-order spot. We are avoiding the temptation to over-leverage against Sale, who keeps **Trea Turner**'s ceiling suppressed at 54.22, but we must stay aggressive elsewhere to capitalize on these high-xERA starters.",
